HST Office: the tab row's feature search box is in the accessibility tree, with a press action.

The box is a child window of the tab control, but VCLXAccessibleTabControl listed only the page tabs
and the banner link, so a screen reader walking the tab row never found it. The tab control's
accessible now lists the windows placed on it after the tabs (the search box, child id
"hst-tab-search", and the banner link) in visual order. The box's accessible is a push button whose
one action, "press", opens the feature search as a click does.

- vcl/source/accessibility/vclxaccessibletabcontrol.cxx, sfx2/source/notebookbar/NotebookbarTabControl.cxx.

